cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Which Preference Gets Measured? Context and Channel Instability in Model Preference Audits"
authors:
  - family-names: Berczi
    given-names: Benji
abstract: >-
  A same-item, multi-channel study of large instruction-tuned models showing that
  forced-choice preference profiles are context- and channel-indexed: explicitly
  non-adopted persona descriptions and matched non-agent normative content shift
  committed choices, while owned preference, self-prediction, choice, and identity
  report can dissociate about the same configuration. Apart Digital Minds Research
  Sprint, Track 5.
keywords:
  - AI welfare
  - model preferences
  - persona
  - construct validity
  - interpretability
repository-code: "https://github.com/benjibrcz/which-preference-gets-measured"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-08-17
